    <bpmn:process id="W_W4084" name="W4084. Frontline Change Champion / Super-User Network Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Major system/process change (ERP, POS, ecommerce, WMS)
Frequency: Per initiative + maintained network
Volume: Champion network (1–2 per store + DC + HQ function; ~250–400 champions)
Owner: OCM Lead / IT Adoption (links to VS-27)
Participants: Champions, store/DC leadership, IT (VS-27), L&amp;D (VS-19.4)
Source: workflow W4084 — Frontline Change Champion / Super-User Network Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4084_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4084_Lane1" name="OCM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4084_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4084_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4084_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4084_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4084_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4084_Start3" name="Major system/process change (ERP, POS, ecommerce, WMS)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4084_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4084_Task4" name="OCM/IT recruit and accredit a super-user/champion network (respected frontline…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: OCM/IT recruit and accredit a super-user/champion network (respected frontline peers per site/function), define their role (peer support, feedback, early adoption), and incentivize
Responsible (R): OCM / IT / Site Leadership
Accountable (A): OCM Lead
Duration: Per initiative</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4084_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4084_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4084_Task5" name="OCM/IT train champions early (ahead of general rollout), give them a direct…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: OCM/IT train champions early (ahead of general rollout), give them a direct channel to the program team, and use them for pilot feedback (links to VS-133 W4061)
Responsible (R): OCM / IT / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): OCM Lead
Duration: Per initiative</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4084_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4084_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4084_Task6" name="OCM/IT sustain the network: recognition, refresh on change, retire when no…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: OCM/IT sustain the network: recognition, refresh on change, retire when no longer needed, and capture peer insights
Responsible (R): OCM / IT
Accountable (A): OCM Lead
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4084_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4084_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
